}. We fit a static BT model to each season, without the time-varying strengths such models can include.\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a[:50]; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"static\\|dynamic\\|time-varying\" paper.tex | head","description":"Weave new citations into anchored paragraphs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":64547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":802},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e124b283-7beb-4c0b-bb14-027f4e696ac4","uuid":"3626b6b9-9142-4e3d-9ab6-57eec6e21bfd","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:15:40.461Z","request_id":"req_011CgVZiUHu7QCRAaZuFUDag"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MRhEYRR48o7i2BeVGJBbeX","type":"tool_result","content":"126:Table~\\ref{tab:cases} lists the cases. The four designs are crowdsourced votes from the Chatbot Arena 140k human-preference release~\\citep{Chiang2024ChatbotAA}; expert human and GPT-4 pairwise judgments of MT-Bench answers~\\citep{Zheng2023JudgingLW}; and NBA games from two seasons of the FiveThirtyEight Elo record, the 2014 and 2015 seasons in that file's labeling, with each game a comparison between two teams, following the long use of BT models for sports tournaments~\\citep{Cattelan2013DynamicBM}. We fit a static BT model to each season, without the time-varying strengths such models can include. Arena ``tie'' and ``both bad'' votes and MT-Bench tie judgments become ties ($y=\\tfrac12$); NBA games have no ties. Each design contributes three cases: drop/top-1, flip/top-1, and drop/top-$k$. With the two controls this gives 17 cases. All method choices were made on disjoint development data: the Arena 55k release and the NBA 1983 season. Any final-split row whose content hash also appears there is excluded; the recorded cross-split overlap is zero. The 17 cases were then run once in a sealed evaluation under seeds 101, 102, and 103. Every episode either returns a set that the evaluator verifies, or counts as a failure; none failed. The evaluation completed and passed all of its validity gates.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e124b283-7beb-4c0b-bb14-027f4e696ac4","uuid":"e46e951f-bfea-4cdc-89bb-f7292d59416f","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:15:40.562Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"126:Table~\\ref{tab:cases} lists the cases. The four designs are crowdsourced votes from the Chatbot Arena 140k human-preference release~\\citep{Chiang2024ChatbotAA}; expert human and GPT-4 pairwise judgments of MT-Bench answers~\\citep{Zheng2023JudgingLW}; and NBA games from two seasons of the FiveThirtyEight Elo record, the 2014 and 2015 seasons in that file's labeling, with each game a comparison between two teams, following the long use of BT models for sports tournaments~\\citep{Cattelan2013DynamicBM}. We fit a static BT model to each season, without the time-varying strengths such models can include. Arena ``tie'' and ``both bad'' votes and MT-Bench tie judgments become ties ($y=\\tfrac12$); NBA games have no ties. Each design contributes three cases: drop/top-1, flip/top-1, and drop/top-$k$. With the two controls this gives 17 cases. All method choices were made on disjoint development data: the Arena 55k release and the NBA 1983 season. Any final-split row whose content hash also appears there is excluded; the recorded cross-split overlap is zero. The 17 cases were then run once in a sealed evaluation under seeds 101, 102, and 103. Every episode either returns a set that the evaluator verifies, or counts as a failure; none failed. The evaluation completed and passed all of its validity gates.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
